{"name":"Angel’s Trumpet","hex":"#f6dd34","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"angel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An incorporeal and holy or semidivine messenger from a deity or other divine entity, traditionally depicted as a youthful, winged figure in flowing robes.\n\n One of the lowest order of such beings, below virtues.","One of the lowest order of such beings, below virtues."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To support by donating money."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/angel"},{"term":"trumpet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A musical instrument of the brass family, generally tuned to the key of B-flat; by extension, any type of lip-vibrated aerophone, most often valveless and not chromatic.","Someone who plays the trumpet; a trumpeter."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sound loudly, be amplified","To play the trumpet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trumpet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Angel's trumpet","blocks":[{"text":"Angel's trumpet may refer to:"},{"items":["two closely related genera of poisonous flowering plants in the family Solanaceae:\nBrugmansia, woody plants with pendulous flowers\nBrugmansia × candida, a widespread garden plant\nDatura, herbaceous plants with erect flowespines","Brugmansia, woody plants with pendulous flowers\nBrugmansia × candida, a widespread garden plant","Brugmansia × candida, a widespread garden plant","Datura, herbaceous plants with erect flowespines",""]},{"items":["Brugmansia, woody plants with pendulous flowers\nBrugmansia × candida, a widespread garden plant","Brugmansia × candida, a widespread garden plant","Datura, herbaceous plants with erect flowespines"]},{"items":["Brugmansia × candida, a widespread garden plant"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angel's_trumpet","wikidata":"Q4762026"},{"title":"Trumpet","blocks":[{"text":"The trumpet is a brass instrument. The most common type of trumpet is a transposing instrument in B♭, with pitches sounding a whole step lower than written. The trumpet family includes instruments ranging from the piccolo trumpet, with the highest register in the brass family, to the bass trumpet, pitched one octave below the standard B♭ or C trumpet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Yamaha_Trumpet_YTR-8335LA_crop.jpg/330px-Yamaha_Trumpet_YTR-8335LA_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trumpet","wikidata":"Q8338"},{"title":"Angel","blocks":[{"text":"An angel is a spiritual, heavenly, or supernatural entity, often depicted as humanoid with bird-like wings, frequently in the role as a messenger or intermediary between God and humanity in various traditions like the Abrahamic religions. Other roles include protectors and guides for humans, such as guardian angels, and servants of God. In Western belief-systems the term is often used to distinguish benevolent from malevolent intermediary beings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Angel_of_the_Annunciation_MET_DP167921.jpg/330px-Angel_of_the_Annunciation_MET_DP167921.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angel","wikidata":"Q235113"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Musicians_at_the_coal_yard_-_DPLA_-_654d5920548ca26c571a5337d7807c60.jpg/500px-Musicians_at_the_coal_yard_-_DPLA_-_654d5920548ca26c571a5337d7807c60.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Musicians_at_the_coal_yard_-_DPLA_-_654d5920548ca26c571a5337d7807c60.jpg/500px-Musicians_at_the_coal_yard_-_DPLA_-_654d5920548ca26c571a5337d7807c60.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Trio of trumpeters in Toledo, Ohio, approximately 1940","link":"https://en.wikipe